.TH MDT.LAYOUT_PATTERN_TYPES 4 2026-11-10 "Lustre" "Lustre Kernel Interfaces"
.SH NAME
mdt.layout_pattern_types \- file layout pattern types advertised to clients
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY
.RI "lctl get_param mdt." FSNAME *.layout_pattern_types
.SY
.RI "lctl set_param mdt." FSNAME *.layout_pattern_types= TYPES
.YS
.SS PROPERTIES
.TP
.B Access Permissions
.br
.BR 644 " | " -rw-r--r--
.TP
.B Scope
.br
Per-MDT device, but clients use the value of MDT0000 only.
.TP
.B Config
.br
.B layout_pattern_types
is always present for MDT devices.
.TP
.B Default
.br
.RB layout_pattern_types= raid0,mdt,overstriped,hole,released
.TP
.B Valid Values
.br
.BR raid0 ", " mdt ", " overstriped ", " hole ", " released ,
.BR parity ", " all ", " default ", " none
.SH DESCRIPTION
The comma-separated list
.I TYPES
of file layout pattern types that this MDT advertises to clients when they
connect.
A client only uses the layout types that both it and the MDT support: the
MDS sends this list in the connect reply, and the client leaves components
whose pattern is not in the list uninitialized, reading another mirror
instead if the file has one.
The list a client was given is visible on that client as
.BR lov.layout_pattern_types (4).
.PP
The pre-2.18 baseline of
.BR raid0 ", " mdt " and " overstriped
is mandatory and is restored whenever it is removed, since every client and
MDS understands those layouts.
The list also shows the
.BR hole " and " released
layout flags, which are part of that baseline.
In practice
.B parity
(erasure coded FLR mirrors, see
.BR lfs-mirror-create (1))
is the only type that can be turned on and off, which lets an administrator
stop advertising EC layouts to new client connections without unmounting
the filesystem.
.PP
A value with no leading operator replaces the current list, keeping the
mandatory baseline.
A leading
.B +
or
.B \-
adds to or removes from the current list, and applies to all following
types up to the next operator.
The value
.B all
enables every type this MDT supports,
.B default
restores the list the MDT starts up with (see
.BR MODULES ),
and
.B none
reverts to the mandatory baseline.
Types that this MDT does not support are ignored, while unrecognized names
return
.BR EINVAL .
.SH MODULES
This parameter is in the following modules:
.EX
.B mdt.*.layout_pattern_types
.EE
The value an MDT starts up with comes from the
.B mdt_enable_flr_ec
parameter of the
.B mdt
module, which adds
.B parity
when set and is off by default.
.SH CAVEATS
The list is negotiated when a client connects and again on every
reconnect, so a change reaches mounted clients the next time they
reconnect.  Layouts a client already holds keep the previous list until
their layout lock is dropped.
.PP
On a filesystem with several MDTs a client takes the list from MDT0000
only and applies it to files on every MDT.  Setting the parameter on
another MDT has no effect on clients, so keep the MDTs in agreement by
setting it on all of them at once, as in the persistent example below.
A persistent setting also reaches an MDT added later, which otherwise
starts from its own
.B mdt_enable_flr_ec
default.
.PP
Removing a type does not change files that already use it.  On a client
that connects afterwards those components are unusable: reading such a
file succeeds only if another mirror is available, writing it marks the
overlapping components stale so that a later resync from a client that
negotiated the type rebuilds them, and resyncing them from this client
fails.
.PP
A client refuses to create a file with a component whose type it did not
negotiate, so removing
.B parity
also stops the clients that reconnect afterwards from creating EC files.
The MDT itself does not enforce the list: a client that did not negotiate,
such as one older than 2.18, can still create an EC layout on request.
.SH EXAMPLES
Advertise EC (parity) layouts on all MDTs of the
.B testfs
filesystem, persistently:
.EX
.RB "mgs# " "lctl set_param -P mdt.testfs-*.layout_pattern_types=+parity"
.EE
Stop advertising EC layouts to clients until MDT0000 restarts, since
clients take the list from MDT0000:
.EX
.RB "mds# " "lctl set_param mdt.testfs-MDT0000.layout_pattern_types=-parity"
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
The
.B layout_pattern_types
parameter is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 2.18.0.
.\" Added in commit v2_17_60
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lfs-mirror-create (1),
.BR lov.layout_pattern_types (4),
.BR lustre.enable_flr_ec (4),
.BR lctl-get_param (8),
.BR lctl-set_param (8)
